# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, regardless
# of the platform/user's core.autocrlf setting -- discovered live while
# validating the Secure Cohort Handshake and Signed Roster Runtime
# slice (docs/secure-cohort-handshake-foundation.md): on a Windows
# checkout with the common core.autocrlf=true setting,
# scripts/generate_protos.sh (the only tracked *.sh file at the time)
# checked out with CRLF line endings; infra/docker/cpp-coordinator.Dockerfile
# and infra/docker/python-worker.Dockerfile both COPY it into a Linux
# build context and run it via `bash scripts/generate_protos.sh`, which
# failed with "set: pipefail: invalid option name" (bash chokes on the
# embedded \r in `set -euo pipefail\r`) -- breaking every Docker Compose
# build of the coordinator/python-worker images from a fresh Windows
# clone. This was a real, previously-undiscovered, repo-wide bug, not
# specific to this slice; fixed here rather than worked around locally.
*.sh text eol=lf
